  "event:evt.gen_43.grain_runs_out": {
   "status": "approved",
   "produced_by": {
    "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
    "skill": "urim-chronologist@5",
    "run": "main"
   },
   "produced_at": "2026-11-02T13:44:25+00:00",
   "agent_notes": [
    "The text gives no length for the interval between the return (Gen 42) and the exhaustion of the grain. Revised after review: 3.5 months with a 1.2-month margin, so the lower bound (about 68 days) clears the two round trips of about 33 days each implied by v. 10; Gen 45:6 (two years of famine so far) is the ceiling. The central value is a guess for a large family with a donkey-load per man. MACRO_ERA because no time word marks it."
   ],
   "history": [
    {
     "status": "changes_requested",
     "at": "2026-11-02T13:43:46+00:00",
     "note": "[should_fix] Keep the lower bound above about 66 days: for example, an offset of 3 months with a 1-month margin, or 3.5 months with 1.5. Cite v. 10 (two round trips of about 33 days each) in temporal_reasoning_note as the floor, and Gen 45:6 as the ceiling. (GEN.43.10: \"except we had lingered, surely now we had returned this second time\" (כִּֽי־עַתָּ֥ה שַׁ֖בְנוּ זֶ֥ה פַעֲמָֽיִם))",
     "by": "urim-critic@3 · claude-opus-5-5"
    },
    {
     "status": "approved",
     "at": "2026-11-02T13:44:58+00:00",
     "note": null,
     "by": "urim-critic@3 · claude-opus-5-5"
    }
   ],
   "source": null
  },
