  "verse.en:GEN.43.11": {
   "status": "draft",
   "produced_by": {
    "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
    "skill": "urim-philologist@1",
    "run": "main"
   },
   "produced_at": "2026-11-02T14:13:08+00:00",
   "agent_notes": [
    "The botanical identifications (נְכֹאת, לֹט, בָּטְנִים) are uncertain; the commentators themselves disagree (Rashi: 'I do not know what they are'). I glossed with the commonly proposed senses (gum tragacanth/spice, ladanum/myrrh, pistachios) and flagged the doubt in the notes. 'Balm' for צֳרִי is the traditional rendering; the plant is unidentified."
   ],
   "history": [],
   "source": null
  },
  "verse.en:GEN.43.12": {
   "status": "draft",
   "produced_by": {
    "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
    "skill": "urim-philologist@1",
    "run": "main"
   },
   "produced_at": "2026-11-02T14:13:08+00:00",
   "agent_notes": [
    "מִשְׁנֶה כֶּסֶף: 'second silver' or 'double silver'. Rashi reads 'twice the first amount'; Radak 'a second silver'. I follow the 'double' sense (a second sum besides the returned money) but this is a judgment call: the repaid silver plus new purchase money."
   ],
   "history": [],
   "source": null
  },
  "verse.en:GEN.43.13": {
   "status": "draft",
   "produced_by": {
    "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
    "skill": "urim-philologist@1",
    "run": "main"
   },
   "produced_at": "2026-11-02T14:15:30+00:00",
   "agent_notes": [],
   "history": [],
   "source": null
  },
  "verse.en:GEN.43.14": {
   "status": "draft",
   "produced_by": {
    "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
    "skill": "urim-philologist@1",
    "run": "main"
   },
   "produced_at": "2026-11-02T14:15:30+00:00",
   "agent_notes": [
    "'Your other brother' (achikhem acher): Rashi and Ramban (citing Genesis Rabbah) read it as Simeon, the 'other' one, or as a half-conscious prayer that Joseph too may live. I render it literally and leave the identification to the commentary. KJV's 'of my children' has no Hebrew basis; the verb shakol has no object here.",
    "El Shaddai: I keep 'God Almighty' in the dramatic layer as the conventional rendering and note Rashi's 'sufficient' wordplay in the commentary only as his reading. The modern etymology of Shaddai is uncertain; I did not claim one."
   ],
   "history": [],
   "source": null
  },
  "verse.en:GEN.43.15": {
   "status": "draft",
   "produced_by": {
    "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
