   "agent_notes": [
    "The steward speaks of 'your God and the God of your father'. Whether he speaks as a convert, a courtier schooled in Joseph's piety (Rashbam) or simply with courtesy is not in the text; the commentary says so. I glossed the Elohim forms as singular God, since the verb nathan is singular.",
    "Ramban explains the 'treasure' via an ordinary grain-market accident; Ibn Ezra via a forgotten hoard. I mention these as readings and do not choose, because the text leaves the cause of the silver unsaid."
   ],
   "history": [],
   "source": null
  },
